# 🎓 CampusOS

> Your Campus. Your Intelligence. Your Future.

CampusOS helps college students act early instead of reacting late. It combines attendance planning, an adaptive study planner, notes search and a career gap analyzer in one dashboard.

**Live demo:** https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/campusos/

## Why CampusOS?
Students juggle attendance rules, deadlines, revision and placements in separate tools. CampusOS puts these together and turns the data into next steps.

## Features
| Module | What it does |
|---|---|
| Attendance | Subject-wise percentage, 75% eligibility, classes you can miss or must attend, "what if" simulator |
| Adaptive planner | Ranks tasks by deadline urgency × effort × attendance risk and builds a daily plan with focus blocks and breaks |
| Notes assistant | TF-IDF search with note and paragraph citations, fill-in-the-blank quiz generation |
| Career gap analyzer | Compares resume and job description skills, gives a readiness score, weekly roadmap and interview questions |
| Analytics | Early-warning risk signal from attendance, overdue tasks and completion rate |

> The risk score is a heuristic signal, not a prediction of exam results.

## Tech
HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript. Data is stored in the browser (`localStorage`). There is no backend or LLM in this version.

## Run locally
```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/campusos.git
cd campusos
python3 -m http.server 8000
```
Open http://localhost:8000

## How the planner ranks tasks
`priority = (3 / (days_to_due + 1)) × hours × (1.5 if subject attendance < 75%)`
Overdue tasks use a weight of 6. Completed tasks drop out, so the plan adapts.

